{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh charged all his people, etc.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 12a) that because the astrologers of Egypt were in doubt whether the redeemer would be born from the Hebrew women or from the Egyptian women, therefore 'he charged all his people.' And this doubt came to them because in truth he was born from the Hebrew women, but it is said of Pharaoh's daughter, 'and he became a son to her' (Exodus 2:10); therefore they thought that perhaps he would be a literal son to some Egyptian woman — in the pattern of the sun and the moon in Joseph's dream (Genesis 37:9–10), where the matter reached even Bilhah."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:17:36.906386593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}